widgets-sapid-heading = Build applications with Sapid
widgets-sapid-description = Glory provides the semantic building blocks. Sapid composes them into application components such as themed buttons, cards, form fields, tabs and dialogs. Start with Sapid when you need a ready-made control, and combine it with Glory views and your own widgets. Both use the same Cage, Bond, Vary and Owner model.
widgets-sapid-setup = This example is compiled with the website. Use matching Glory and Sapid revisions and follow the Sapid repository's stylesheet and host setup. Each showcase guide records its host support; check the widget you plan to use when targeting Web, SSR or native hosts.
