custom-widgets-sapid-heading = Compose with existing Sapid components
custom-widgets-sapid-description = Check the Sapid widget guides before implementing a new control. Your component can combine a Sapid form field, button or card with ordinary Glory views and business state. Keep that state in the build Scope, pass Cage or Bond values to component properties, and let the existing Owner lifecycle manage subscriptions and cleanup.
styling-sapid-heading = Use Sapid themes for component styling
styling-sapid-description = Sapid's Theme, palettes, variants and sizes provide coordinated component styling. Choose a theme for control colors and states, then use Glory styles or application classes for the surrounding layout. Follow the showcase's stylesheet setup and per-widget host support when applying the same design on another renderer.
