# Direct display API, current main revision
display-nav = XML DSL & templates
display-meta-title = XML DSL and display templates — Glory
display-meta-description = Build browser views with Glory view!, shared HTML templates, components, keyed Each, Show and owned field bindings.
display-title = XML DSL and display templates
display-lead = Use optional XML syntax or handwritten configuration to build browser views on the same shared HTML template runtime. Cage, Bond and Vary provide owned fine-grained updates.
display-layers-title = Two layers, shared reactivity
display-layers-body = HTML/CSS is the display contract. Lowercase HTML in view! creates shared static templates and dynamic slots; a raw <button> does not implicitly create a semantic Button Widget. Runtime records cover actual instances, ranges, dynamic targets, events and references. Physical DOM nodes still exist. Higher-level semantic widgets and Sapid remain a separate layer with their own host integrations.
display-install-title = Enable the optional DSL
display-imports-body = Import glory::display::prelude::* for the direct display API. Keep it separate from glory::prelude::*, whose App, Scope, view and each belong to the semantic Widget API. dsl adds view!, template!, field! and the optional #[component] compiler; handwritten templates need only web.
display-counter-title = A component and its browser root
display-bindings-body = #[component] generates a Component implementation and a concrete Props type. The injected &Scope owns the Cage. {"{"}count{"}"} subscribes to the handle; {"{"}count.get(){"}"} reads once; {"{"}move || ...{"}"} tracks a computed binding. The click callback takes no browser event parameter. Ordinary functions can also return View values. Component macros currently require synchronous functions and concrete Props types.
display-start-body = Build the library for wasm32-unknown-unknown and run wasm-bindgen with the matching locked version, as in the Web guide. In your wasm-bindgen start function, call launch() and retain its returned display::App in application storage. The HTML needs an empty element with id="app". This entry mounts browser CSR; it does not adopt a semantic SSR snapshot.
display-handwritten-title = The same runtime without XML
display-handwritten-body = A static Template declares HTML and named fields; view(&TEMPLATE) supplies live configuration. The XML frontend lowers to this same API and sparse host. Template compilation is shared across instances, and static elements do not each allocate a semantic Widget record.
display-structure-title = Keyed rows and conditional content
display-keyed-body = KeyedList stores each business value once and separates order notifications from row data. Each owns row scopes and field projections. Moves and same-key replacements retain member identity; removal and reinsertion create a new generation. update_key edits a row without notifying order readers. Keys must remain stable and duplicate keys are rejected. display::Each and ui::Each share reconciliation, with distinct host and row models.
display-content-body = Show retires its hidden branch; showing it again creates fresh branch state. Content value={"{"}...{"}"} composes views, Option/Vec, fragments and component children; ordinary {"{"}expr{"}"} remains text. class:danger={"{"}...{"}"} toggles a boolean class slot. Components and content ranges can own scopes; static HTML descendants do not each need one.
display-boundary-title = Current display support
display-boundary-body = At this revision the direct display host supports browser CSR: div/span/button/a/h1/table/tbody/tr/td, text, bounded static attributes, dynamic class/title/aria-label, class toggles and parameterless click. SSR/hydration, Blitz, full event/property coverage and controlled input/IME have not migrated to this host. The existing semantic Widget API continues to provide its Web/SSR/native capabilities. The display host batches changes in a microtask after the JavaScript turn; semantic WebApp uses its own frame lifecycle.
display-semantic-link = Continue with semantic widgets →
display-home-link = Explore XML views and shared templates →
platforms-mobile-title = Android and iOS · semantic widgets
platforms-mobile-body = The shared mobile counter has explicit NativeActivity/GameActivity and UIKit entries with packaged assets and host-specific lifecycle/input checks. Use the mobile example for platform setup; direct XML display views have no mobile adapter yet.
platforms-mobile-link = Read the pinned mobile example ↗

display-widget-guide-title = Semantic Widget API
display-widget-guide-body = This guide uses semantic widgets and their Web/SSR/native integrations. For view! and shared HTML templates, use the display guide. The direct display host currently supports browser CSR; its SSR/hydration, native and controlled-input migrations remain pending.
